Z||000028||LZeitgeist||05-30-2001||09:32 AM||||CAUTION: RANT AHEAD<P><BR>Galen sez:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I like my section of the hills..  we got some nice fiero owners down here. plus they come to me lookin for help so all is cool  I think hehe..<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Great! Then why are you always whining about what we're doing in Raleigh?<P>Damn, if you don't want to drive where the stuff is going on, then do stuff with the people closer to you. I've owned Fieros for ten years, and it's just been the last year that I've found any events of *any* kind anywhere near me. Up until six months ago, the closest thing to Raleigh was southeast Virginia, which is an excellent distance for an event, but too far (for my personal taste) for monthly meetings. <P>There *is* (or at least used to be) a group that met in northern South Carolina. Seems to me it was somewhat close to Charlotte NC, but I don't recall exactly. I remember that for me, it was a tossup between there and southeast Virginia, and the Virginia group seemed a bit closer to Raleigh than the SC group.<P>Don't expect a Fiero group to show up on your doorstep and pick you up to take you for a ride unless you start the group yourself and hold the meetings at your house. If you want to be part of the Greensboro area group, then put a little effort into the experience like the rest of us are. If you're 70 miles east of Charlotte, you're closer to the Greensboro group than we are in Raleigh, and *we* have no problems getting to G'boro every other month. If you don't want to drive this far, then find something closer. But cripes, quit whining about it already.<P>(And no, I'm *not* speaking on behalf of the Greensboro group - that's Bob's baby. I'm speaking on nobody's behalf but my own.)||||reg||1
Z||000029||Galen||05-30-2001||04:14 PM||||Well your behalf can just go on elsewhere, I ask for none of it. How am I closer to Greensboro than Raleigh? Go look at a map, Rockingham is on the state line.. thats a lil far. Come back when you know what you're talking about.. and dont prove to be an idiot.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000030||LZeitgeist||05-30-2001||05:31 PM||||Galen - <BR>At least I can appreciate what Bob has done for Fieros in the state, actively participate, and not whine like a 5-year old child because the get-togethers don't happen on my doorstep. A$$hole. <P>I think maybe it's a good thing that you are too damn lazy to participate in the Greensboro group. I know more than one person involved that would just as soon you stayed away. <P>Start your own group in Rockingham, jerk. And quit giving Bob a hard time about what boils down to *your* laziness. He doesn't deserve it. ||||reg||1
Z||000031||bHooper||05-30-2001||05:41 PM||||ok, here go's!  Galen (Rae qwan, whatever you choopsed to be called)... get off of your ASS and pick a spot, and say "Hey guys I have this coold restaurant that we all can go to and look at cars and eat lunch and talk Fiero stuff, together.  It's close to XYZ highway, in the town of BFE, with plenty of cheap gas and cool roads to go driving on.  I think it would be a great spot for everyone to come and visit!"<P>Now doesn't that sound so much better than your CONSTANT bitchin and whining about how we never go south!  Did you ever think that the reason we never go south, is that no one (not even Brian Wilkinson (who lives in Charlotte, btw)) suggest a place and time!  <P>I mean, why should we go down there if we don't have a spot to go to?!  When we all met in Hickory, we had people from Sylva (2 hours), Atlanta (4 hours.. or more), Raleigh (3.5 hours), Tri-City's of Tennesee (3 hours), Greensboro (1.5 hours) and Hickory.  Oh yeah, and Brian W. drove to Greensboro, from Charlotte first! <P>You see, complaining doesn't work... action does.  <P>What, do you never leave that little town that you live in?  That's ok, if so.  However, it does kinda limit your exposure to the world.<P>Have you ever riddin on a plane, or been in a train?  Ever go out onto the great Atlantic Ocean, or see the beautifull Parkway?<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
