Z||000043||FieroHarry||05-31-2001||04:12 PM||||Chris,<BR>FOCOSEVA has members all over the place we dont care what state you live in, we just love Fiero's.<BR>I would point out that Bob Englet and a few others have started a club for NC and seem to be doing very well (Bob I say that because I havent gotten my lazy duff down there and attended one yet but will very soon).<BR>Bob is also a member of FOCOSEVA <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I think it would do the NC club good to have another member who wants to get out there and meet people....... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The choice is yours to make and I wouldnt do anything to try and take any memebrs away from Bob.<BR>But you could belong to both  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> then you could get our news letter.<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000044||Bob Englert||05-31-2001||08:38 PM||||Chris:<P>By all means join both groups.  The Southeast VA group is much more established and active and they have a lot of great Fiero folks.  Our NC group has no officers, no dues, no newsletter, and hopefully no stress, ... (doesn't sound like much when I put it that way!!!).  We are just a group that tries to meet somewhere about once per month to share lunch and talk Fieros.  I would like to do a couple of cruises during the summer like we are talking about here if anyone is interested.  <P>Sounds like July 14th is coming together as the date of choice....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
